Malformed component content is now ignored by default. Parsing exceptions are recorded in the component's ``errors`` attribute instead of being raised. To enable the previous strict behavior globally, set ``Component.ignore_exceptions = False`` before parsing and restore it afterward as needed. This is a process-wide class setting, and subclassing ``Calendar`` does not change the component classes created by the parser's component factory. Strict mode still tolerates malformed ``X-*`` property values through the parser's existing special case. See the :ref:`upgrade guide <upgrade-8.0.0-parsing-errors>` for examples. @Pr1meGG
